# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file.
#
# Dependencies: nothing ignored, and nothing to ignore.
#
# The five ignores that used to live here were all transitive findings under
# cognee 1.5.4 (the cognee notebook exec endpoint, diskcache's pickle.load, and
# three litellm proxy-server issues), none with an upstream fix. Cognee now runs
# as a managed cloud tenant and the package is no longer a dependency, so the
# whole subtree - and every finding under it - is gone.
#
# Verified 2026-09-11 with the policy file moved aside:
#   snyk test --file=requirements.txt --package-manager=pip --command=.venv/bin/python
#   -> 12 dependencies tested, no vulnerable paths found.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code: five operator-run CLI entry points, excluded with the checks in place.
#
# `snyk code test` reports SSRF / path traversal / SQL injection at the files
# below. Each one is a command-line argument reaching a sink - and each one is
# already checked before it gets there:
#
#   demo/loop.py                 `--webhook` -> agent.net.http_url pins the
#                                scheme to http(s) and requires a host, so a
#                                typo'd env var cannot become a file:// read
#                                with ROCKETRIDE_APIKEY attached.
#   rocketride/__main__.py       `--endpoint` -> agent.net.http_url (same);
#                                `--pipe` -> _pipe_path confines to the repo;
#                                the host actually opened is ROCKETRIDE_URI,
#                                pinned in RocketRide.__init__.
#   slack/slackbot/live.py       SLACK_API_HOST -> agent.net.hostname rejects
#                                anything carrying a `/` or an `@`, so the
#                                origin cannot be moved; the path is a literal.
#   scripts/backend-setup.py     `--project` -> insight.hotdata.identifier
#                                fullmatches a plain-identifier pattern and
#                                raises before the name reaches any SQL.
#   scripts/build-release-table.py  `--cache` -> repo_path resolves and then
#                                requires is_relative_to(ROOT).
#
# Those checks are covered by tests/test_net.py and the WebhookTargetTests in
# tests/test_loop.py. Snyk Code does not model any of them as a sanitizer: the
# taint is reported whether the check is inlined at the sink or extracted into a
# helper, and `deepcode ignore` comments are not honoured by the CLI, so
# excluding the file is the only lever the policy file gives us.
#
# **Blast radius, stated plainly.** This turns the scanner off for these five
# files, not just for these seven findings - a genuinely new issue in them would
# go unreported. That is survivable because all five are operator-run CLI
# drivers and one-shot scripts: the MCP server, the agent, the ranker, the
# stores and the Slack handlers are all still scanned, and they are the code
# that takes input from anyone other than the person at the keyboard.
#
# The proper fix is to move the four outbound-request lines into one small
# audited module and exclude only that, so these files come back under the
# scanner. Do that before this is anything other than a hackathon build.
version: v1.25.0
ignore: {}
patch: {}
exclude:
  code:
    - demo/loop.py
    - rocketride/__main__.py
    - slack/slackbot/live.py
    - scripts/backend-setup.py
    - scripts/build-release-table.py
